window.products.push({"id":115687,"name":"W10528947 Maytag Washer Drive Hub Kit W10396887 Easy to Install MVWX655DW1 WTW5000DW1 MVWC565FW1 MVWX655DW2 WTW5000DW0 WTW5000DW2 WTW5000DW3 MVWC415EW","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":9.95,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61YKHR9Y+cL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"💡 Maytag Part W10528947 - A high-quality exact equivalent for part numbers AP5665171, 2684908, PS6012095, W10396887, W10528947VP. Ultra Durable W10528947 Drive Hub Kit is compatible with Whirlpool, Admiral, Amana, Crosley, Inglis, Kenmore, Maytag appliances. Maytag Washer Part W10528947 is an essential component of of the washing machine that connects the spin basket to the spin shaft that spins the basket. 🔧 DIY eTips Included - Not sure how to replace the part? Helpful information can be found on the page below. Scroll down to get more repair tips. Acquire valuable skills during the DIY repair project. Maytag Washer W10528947 Hub Kit will help if your appliance does not agitate, spins slowly, is noisy, or pumps but will not spin. Before installing this part, make sure to unplug the washer. Additionally, it is recommended to wear gloves to protect your hands during the installation process. 💡 Whirlpool Hub W10528947 is made of high-quality materials, which makes it durable and long-lasting. Maytag W10528947 is designed to fit snugly into the washing machine and withstand the stress of continuous use. Whirlpool W10528947 Hub is also designed to reduce noise and vibration during operation, which makes it an excellent choice for households. Drive Hub W10528947 Kit meets or exceeds all manufacturer specifications. We provide a lifetime warranty and guarantee 100% money back. 💡How to replace the drive hub on a Whirlpool washer? Replacing the Washer Hub W10528947 can be a DIY project for those with some mechanical experience. The process typically involves removing the washer's agitator, disconnecting the old hub, and installing the new Whirlpool Washing Machine Hub W10528947 in its place. It is important to follow the instructions carefully and use the correct tools to ensure a safe and effective replacement. To access the repair tips, simply scroll down the page. 💡 Will replacing the hub quiet down the noisy spin cycle? Replacing the hub may potentially help to reduce noise during the spin cycle of a washing machine. However, it is important to note that there could be other factors contributing to the noise, such as worn bearings, belts, or other components. It is recommended to inspect and replace any damaged or worn parts in addition to the hub to ensure optimal performance and reduce noise during operation.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61YKHR9Y+cL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"PartsBroz","source_asin":"B07VJFT681","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-115687","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07VJFT681","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B07VJFT681","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
